{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 3066 patch set 2 got LLM-Review -1 for 1 blocking issue, reported twice: the create reroute skipped the rebar-id label-write guard (G6) that the deleted `_apply_one` ran before each dispatch.\n\nPatch set 3 (5bc443bdd96) fixes it:\n- New `batch_dispatch._audited_dispatch(batch, ctx)` runs the guard, loaded from `rebar_id_audit`, then `_dispatch_with_backstop`.\n- The create reroute now calls it after `before_dispatch()`.\n- The coordinator route's `dispatch_fn` uses the same helper instead of its inline copy, so there is 1 guard path.\n- A guard refusal raises and aborts the pass before the vendor is called, as it did on the old loop.\n\nTests:\n- The order test now asserts abort_check → recheck → `audit:outbound_create` → dispatch for each create.\n- New `test_rebar_id_guard_refusal_stops_a_create_before_the_vendor`.\n\nGates:\n- complexity `new=0 increased=0`;\n- `batch_dispatch.py` is 737 LOC;\n- reconciler unit plus integration suites: 3683 passed;\n- full `make verify` exited 0 (19700 passed, 86 skipped).\n\nThe old loop's `_print_batch_recon` RECON line is still not emitted for reroute-dispatched creates. The production create path already ran through the reroute before this change, so it did not emit that line then either."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792670721097856808,"uuid":"a7831c26-224d-49ef-832e-f06eecb53403"}